--TEST--
neither way of writing a command line reaches `Core\Process::run` — the whole shell string is one argument short of the signature and a packed argument list is not an `array<string>`, so nothing is escaped because there is nothing to escape into — `rule:core-classes/process-run`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:core-classes/process-run`: there is no command-line form of this member anywhere in the
// surface, so both of the ways a port would reach for one are refused while
// compiling rather than escaped at run time.

// The whole shell string as the program's name. It is one argument short of
// the member's signature, which is the shape that makes it unwritable: `run`
// has nowhere for a command line to go on its own.
var $whole = Core\Process::run("sh -c 'echo hi'");

// The name separated from its arguments, with the arguments still packed into
// one string. `array<string>` is what the second slot is, so a `string` there
// is refused for its type rather than for its content.
var $packed = Core\Process::run("sh", "-c echo hi");

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0402]: expected 2 argument(s), found 1
  --> case.nvs:9:14
%A
error[E0401]: expected `array<string>`, found `string`
   --> case.nvs:14:39
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
